The case on both sides in Idaho is whether Medicaid work requirements that start January 1st will leave eligible people covered.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:09.940
House Bill 913 set that date for rules the state calls federally mandated.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:22.140
Legislators have said eligible Idahoans will not lose care, and the Idaho Capitol Sun Commentary records their reason as eligibility itself, including a medical frailty exemption for serious illness.

00:03:22.700 --> 00:03:32.100
